IMPORT prelude

-- Racial Discrimination Act 1975 (Cth), with the complaint provisions of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986
-- -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR) and the prelude's elem, not the daydate library. The AHRC Act counts in months ("more than 24 months after
-- the alleged acts ... took place", s 46PH(1)(b)) and in plain days ("within 60 days after the date of issue of the
-- notice", s 46PO(2)). Both are counted by the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Compilation No. 39, compilation date 28 March
-- 2026, deposited at subjects/au/acts-interpretation-act-1901/registers/source-bundle/C1901A00002.txt): s 2G(2) (a period
-- of 2 or more months), s 36(1) item 6 (a period "after" a day leaves that day out) and s 36(2), (3) (a last day on a
-- Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday). Saturday and Sunday are computed; holidays are an input (a list of dates), since no
-- holiday calendar is deposited.
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Racial Discrimination Act 1975 and the AHRC Act complaint provisions`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- The number of days in a calendar month.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The last day of a period of n calendar months (n of 2 or more) that begins after a given day.
-- AIA s 36(1) item 6: a period "expressed to begin after a specified day ... does not include that day", so it starts the
-- next day. AIA s 2G(2): "a reference to a period of 2 or more months is a reference to a period: (a) starting at the start
-- of a day of one of the calendar months (the starting month); and (b) ending: (i) immediately before the start of the
-- corresponding day of the calendar month that is that number of calendar months after the starting month; or (ii) if
-- there is no such day -- at the end of the calendar month that is that number of calendar months after the starting
-- month." So the last day is the day before the corresponding day, or the last day of that month where the corresponding
-- day does not exist (an act on 28 February 2022 starts the period on 1 March 2022; the last day is 29 February 2024; an
-- act on 28 February 2024 starts it on 29 February 2024; February 2026 has no 29th, so the last day is 28 February 2026).
-- Fork F7 in NOTES.md.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of` n `months beginning after` `the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `the start` GREATER THAN `the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY (`the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`) `the month` `the year`
    ELSE `the date` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` (DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the start`) `the month` `the year`)
    WHERE
        `the start` MEANS `the date` 1 `days after` `the day`
        `the count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the start` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the month index` MEANS `the count` MODULO 12
        `the year` MEANS (`the count` MINUS `the month index`) DIVIDED BY 12
        `the month` MEANS `the month index` PLUS 1

-- The day of the week, 0 for Monday to 6 for Sunday, counted from Monday 1 January 1900.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekday of` d MEANS (DATE_SERIAL d MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1900)) MODULO 7

-- AIA s 36(2), (3): "If: (a) an Act requires or allows a thing to be done; and (b) the last day for doing the thing is a
-- Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday; then the thing may be done on the next day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a
-- holiday." "holiday, in relation to the time for doing a thing, means: (a) a day that is a public holiday in the place in
-- which the thing is to be or may be done; and (b) if the thing is to be or may be done at a particular office or other
-- place -- a day on which the place or office is closed for the whole day." The holidays are the caller's list.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday` d holidays IF
        `the weekday of` d AT LEAST 5
    OR elem d holidays

-- From a last day, step forward one day at a time to the first day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday (the
-- last day itself if it is none of those).
GIVEN d IS A DATE, holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day from` d `that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday, given` holidays MEANS
    IF `is a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday` d holidays
    THEN `the first day from` (`the date` 1 `days after` d) `that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday, given` holidays
    ELSE d
